1
00:00:01,835 --> 00:00:05,438
Is it done yet? Is it done yet?

2
00:00:05,505 --> 00:00:06,740
Not yet? Akira?

3
00:00:08,108 --> 00:00:09,376
It's coming along nicely.

4
00:00:09,442 --> 00:00:10,844
I can't wait any longer.

5
00:00:10,910 --> 00:00:12,746
Here's the first one.

6
00:00:14,514 --> 00:00:16,883
- It smells great.
- Open your mouth.

7
00:00:18,985 --> 00:00:20,053
Yum! It's delicious.

8
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:21,554
- Is it?
- Yes.

9
00:00:21,621 --> 00:00:24,457
Then, here is the second one.

10
00:00:26,793 --> 00:00:30,663
Now. Which one was the special short rib?

11
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:34,434
I don't know.

12
00:00:34,501 --> 00:00:38,071
You are hopeless. First class people
knows first class things.

13
00:00:38,138 --> 00:00:42,675
If you can't recognize this
you can't call yourself the best surgeon!

14
00:00:43,109 --> 00:00:44,644
- I'll taste it for you.
- OK.

15
00:00:46,846 --> 00:00:48,648
Isn't it good? Let me taste it, too.

16
00:00:48,715 --> 00:00:51,084
- All right. All right.
- I want it so bad.

17
00:00:51,151 --> 00:00:53,987
- You'd better get it right this time.
- One more time!

18
00:00:58,491 --> 00:00:59,592
This is good meat.

19
00:01:00,093 --> 00:01:03,696
I heard you've restructured
the hospital's system.

20
00:01:03,763 --> 00:01:04,631
Yes.

21
00:01:05,031 --> 00:01:08,268
Then why are the public
evaluation ratings still so low?

22
00:01:08,334 --> 00:01:10,570
I deeply apologise.

23
00:01:11,171 --> 00:01:15,241
I'm not sure your decision
to broadcast an operation

24
00:01:15,308 --> 00:01:16,409
was a good idea.

25
00:01:16,476 --> 00:01:20,080
What we want is to improve dignity.

26
00:01:20,146 --> 00:01:21,081
Indeed.

27
00:01:21,915 --> 00:01:23,483
Do you have any plans coming up?

28
00:01:24,517 --> 00:01:27,487
- A plan...Of course, sir.
- We would love to hear that.

29
00:01:27,554 --> 00:01:33,359
Well, may I ask you
to discuss this matter...another time.

30
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:38,331
Today, we have prepared
some good sweets for you.

31
00:01:39,432 --> 00:01:40,867
- Shiromizu,
- Yes, sir.

32
00:01:43,803 --> 00:01:45,305
Excuse me.

33
00:01:45,371 --> 00:01:47,273
Please, help yourselves.

34
00:01:49,609 --> 00:01:50,743
Sweets.

35
00:01:53,012 --> 00:01:54,547
5,000 sweets.

36
00:01:56,683 --> 00:01:58,485
$10,000

37
00:01:59,986 --> 00:02:01,154
- Hiruma.
- Yes.

38
00:02:01,588 --> 00:02:04,924
This is not the era to do this anymore.

39
00:02:05,325 --> 00:02:06,893
- Huh?
- Indeed.

40
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:10,130
These old ideas that you have,
could be the reason

41
00:02:10,196 --> 00:02:13,233
our hospital's reputation
isn't going well.

42
00:02:13,299 --> 00:02:14,567
Huh? No wait...

43
00:02:14,634 --> 00:02:17,370
I deeply apologise for showing you
an unpleasant scene.

44
00:02:17,437 --> 00:02:20,707
Let us recall those,
poisonous sweets at once.

45
00:02:24,244 --> 00:02:26,646
Hey wait a minute.

46
00:02:32,952 --> 00:02:34,988
Make sure I'm getting them back, OK?

47
00:02:35,054 --> 00:02:37,891
You should be worried
about your blood sugar level.

48
00:02:37,957 --> 00:02:41,161
- Oh, boy, oh boy! I'm so excited.
- Make sure you get it this time.

49
00:02:48,568 --> 00:02:51,571
I got it!
I'm sure this is the special short rib.

50
00:02:51,638 --> 00:02:53,640
- Wrong!
- What?

51
00:02:53,706 --> 00:02:55,341
Why?

52
00:02:58,278 --> 00:02:59,512
What is this?

53
00:02:59,579 --> 00:03:01,581
These are Shitake mushrooms!

54
00:03:02,048 --> 00:03:03,316
It's out of question.

55
00:03:03,917 --> 00:03:07,253
You can't even distinguish

56
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:09,055
vegetables from meat.

57
00:03:09,122 --> 00:03:12,458
You ate all the meat. I am pissed!

58
00:03:12,525 --> 00:03:15,061
Excuse me! Excuse me.

59
00:03:15,428 --> 00:03:16,529
Excuse me.

60
00:03:17,030 --> 00:03:20,300
This special boneless short rib,
special boneless sirloin,

61
00:03:20,366 --> 00:03:21,434
special tender beef,

62
00:03:21,501 --> 00:03:23,836
bring me all of the specials. Thank you!

63
00:03:23,903 --> 00:03:25,405
- Got it!
- So there!

64
00:03:27,941 --> 00:03:29,075
I think I'll try this...

65
00:03:29,142 --> 00:03:30,710
What a greedy wench.

66
00:03:31,911 --> 00:03:32,745
Say what?

67
00:03:32,812 --> 00:03:36,950
Wanting everything...
is proof of having a needy heart.

68
00:03:38,918 --> 00:03:40,920
You seem poorer than I do.

69
00:03:40,987 --> 00:03:43,056
Thinking all expensive things are good,

70
00:03:43,122 --> 00:03:45,191
is a sign of having a bad head.

71
00:03:46,759 --> 00:03:49,295
Honey, don't say that.

72
00:03:50,897 --> 00:03:53,866
You're young, so you must eat your full.

73
00:03:55,168 --> 00:03:56,369
I apologise.

74
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:02,675
Akira, did you hear that?

75
00:04:03,576 --> 00:04:04,410
What?

76
00:04:05,578 --> 00:04:08,248
She said I'm young!

77
00:04:08,715 --> 00:04:10,483
You've become easier, you know.

78
00:04:10,550 --> 00:04:12,452
I hadn't heard it in a while.

79
00:04:12,518 --> 00:04:15,088
Another shochu with tonic water!

80
00:04:15,521 --> 00:04:18,625
<i>This is the story of</i>
<i>a female maverick doctor.</i>

81
00:04:18,691 --> 00:04:19,759
It's good!

82
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:24,897
<i>In 2016, the once sacrosanct university</i>
<i>medical system was in crisis.</i>

83
00:04:25,832 --> 00:04:30,203
<i>The system on which lives depend</i>
<i>had strayed away from what it should be.</i>

84
00:04:31,571 --> 00:04:34,474
<i>The director will now...</i>

85
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:36,342
<i>begin to make his rounds.</i>

86
00:04:37,777 --> 00:04:40,813
From now on, we will come up with

87
00:04:41,447 --> 00:04:45,218
new branding strategies
focusing on the wealthy.

88
00:04:45,285 --> 00:04:47,620
Choose your patients carefully.

89
00:04:47,687 --> 00:04:48,788
- Yes sir.
- Good.

90
00:04:50,957 --> 00:04:51,991
Take a look at them.

91
00:04:52,759 --> 00:04:56,162
We shouldn't even bother
accepting patients like them.

92
00:04:56,229 --> 00:04:57,597
- Yes sir.
- Yes sir.

93
00:04:57,664 --> 00:04:58,665
- Yes sir.
- Yes sir.

94
00:05:00,366 --> 00:05:03,002
Don't get us wrong. We're not
speaking about the hospital.

95
00:05:03,903 --> 00:05:06,139
- Have you lost your way?
- Yes.

96
00:05:06,205 --> 00:05:10,009
I can see how you can get lost.
This is a pretty big hospital. Take care.

97
00:05:10,076 --> 00:05:11,978
<i>Famous hospitals use...</i>

98
00:05:12,045 --> 00:05:14,180
<i>their brand power to push into the world.</i>

99
00:05:14,647 --> 00:05:19,052
<i>On the other hand, highly skilled surgeons</i>
<i>in pursuit of a higher salary</i>

100
00:05:19,118 --> 00:05:21,287
<i>were relocating to foreign countries.</i>

101
00:05:21,988 --> 00:05:24,857
<i>The world of medicine has entered into</i>

102
00:05:25,291 --> 00:05:29,295
<i>the global world</i>
<i>of survival of the fittest.</i>

103
00:05:31,164 --> 00:05:33,966
Dr. Arai from Nijikawamura medical centre.

104
00:05:34,033 --> 00:05:35,068
Never heard of him.

105
00:05:35,134 --> 00:05:38,538
He told us to
absolutely count on you, Dr. Kikawada.

106
00:05:39,439 --> 00:05:40,273
Is that so?

107
00:05:42,008 --> 00:05:43,042
Let's have a look.

108
00:05:44,310 --> 00:05:48,715
A shadow was found on my large intestine
during the physical exam at our village.

109
00:05:48,781 --> 00:05:51,617
They sounded like
it may be rather troublesome...

110
00:05:53,486 --> 00:05:54,387
I see.

111
00:05:55,321 --> 00:05:56,155
Doctor?

112
00:06:00,593 --> 00:06:02,628
I recommend hospitalisation right away.

113
00:06:02,695 --> 00:06:03,629
Hospitalisation?

114
00:06:05,064 --> 00:06:06,499
I'm screwed.

115
00:06:06,899 --> 00:06:09,569
There's no need to get so upset.

116
00:06:09,635 --> 00:06:12,705
Since we're finally here,
let's check in and get a decent treatment.

117
00:06:12,772 --> 00:06:16,442
I will write you a referral form
for our partner hospital.

118
00:06:17,043 --> 00:06:17,977
Pardon?

119
00:06:20,046 --> 00:06:23,216
I'm sorry, our hospital is currently full.

120
00:06:24,484 --> 00:06:26,018
Is it a matter of money?

121
00:06:27,787 --> 00:06:31,824
Can we not receive treatment...
in this hospital if we are not rich?

122
00:06:32,792 --> 00:06:35,061
By no means.

123
00:06:35,495 --> 00:06:36,829
Our hospital is full.

124
00:06:36,896 --> 00:06:38,998
Don't be so unreasonable.

125
00:06:39,065 --> 00:06:40,533
But Dear...

126
00:06:41,567 --> 00:06:42,902
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

127
00:06:44,837 --> 00:06:47,640
Dr. Kikawada, Dr. Kanemoto has arrived.

128
00:06:47,707 --> 00:06:48,541
My goodness.

129
00:06:51,644 --> 00:06:53,579
I will make the call for you, don't worry.

130
00:06:58,418 --> 00:06:59,519
<i>In the midst of it,</i>

131
00:06:59,852 --> 00:07:01,554
<i>a new breed of doctor has emerged.</i>

132
00:07:01,988 --> 00:07:02,955
<i>Freelance doctors,</i>

133
00:07:03,523 --> 00:07:06,592
<i>In other words, maverick doctors.</i>

134
00:07:17,336 --> 00:07:18,171
Who's that.

135
00:07:18,504 --> 00:07:20,440
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

136
00:07:21,107 --> 00:07:22,141
<i>She hates groups,</i>

137
00:07:22,809 --> 00:07:23,910
<i>authority, and…</i>

138
00:07:24,510 --> 00:07:26,045
<i>being controlled.</i>

139
00:07:26,579 --> 00:07:31,451
<i>Her medical license and experience</i>
<i>are her only weapons.</i>

140
00:07:43,663 --> 00:07:44,597
Dr. Kanemoto,

141
00:07:45,965 --> 00:07:47,366
we've been waiting for you.

142
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:49,302
We've been waiting for you.

143
00:07:51,170 --> 00:07:52,572
This way please.

144
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:54,774
We're late.

145
00:07:54,841 --> 00:07:56,776
Hurry up or we'll never
hear the end of this.

146
00:08:02,582 --> 00:08:05,451
Welcome, Dr. Kanemoto!

147
00:08:07,620 --> 00:08:12,191
Hey. Don't you make a big fuss.
My hospitalization is strictly in secret.

148
00:08:12,258 --> 00:08:13,993
A secret?

149
00:08:15,094 --> 00:08:15,962
Daimon!

150
00:08:16,796 --> 00:08:17,864
Who are you?

151
00:08:18,631 --> 00:08:20,433
I'm Surgeon Michiko Daimon.

152
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:21,968
Surgeon?

153
00:08:22,735 --> 00:08:24,470
Exposing your legs like that?

154
00:08:24,537 --> 00:08:26,472
What happened to the
dignity of this hospital?

155
00:08:26,539 --> 00:08:27,507
We're very sorry.

156
00:08:27,573 --> 00:08:29,809
Please, come this way.

157
00:08:37,283 --> 00:08:38,117
Oh, hey.

158
00:08:42,421 --> 00:08:43,923
- Let me see.
- What?

159
00:08:44,323 --> 00:08:45,157
That.

160
00:09:01,641 --> 00:09:03,709
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

161
00:09:04,443 --> 00:09:05,411
<i>Also known as</i>

162
00:09:05,945 --> 00:09:07,446
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

163
00:09:29,302 --> 00:09:33,539
I apologise for causing you
trouble with the sudden request.

164
00:09:33,606 --> 00:09:35,575
Please, don't worry about that.

165
00:09:36,442 --> 00:09:38,578
Although there will be examinations,

166
00:09:38,644 --> 00:09:43,115
you are welcome to stay at our hospital,
for as long as you want.

167
00:09:43,182 --> 00:09:45,952
Oh really? I appreciate your offer.

168
00:09:46,018 --> 00:09:49,989
This is... nothing special, but...

169
00:09:50,056 --> 00:09:51,757
How thoughtful of you.

170
00:09:52,858 --> 00:09:55,728
I'm not sure if you'll like it though.

171
00:09:57,063 --> 00:10:00,666
Look how cute you look on these.

172
00:10:01,267 --> 00:10:03,402
I get a lot of compliments from everyone.

173
00:10:03,970 --> 00:10:05,571
Still, I'm nothing compared to

174
00:10:06,906 --> 00:10:10,009
this charming Mr. Fukuzawa.

175
00:10:11,510 --> 00:10:15,281
Well, it's difficult to say
which of the two is better.

176
00:10:16,816 --> 00:10:18,284
Is that so?

177
00:10:18,351 --> 00:10:21,387
I'll accept it without reservation.

178
00:10:21,454 --> 00:10:23,122
After all, I love Tokyo.

179
00:10:24,056 --> 00:10:25,124
- Yes?
- Excuse me.

180
00:10:25,858 --> 00:10:26,792
What is it?

181
00:10:30,062 --> 00:10:30,997
Director Hiruma.

182
00:10:32,431 --> 00:10:34,000
- Saionji,
- Yes?

183
00:10:34,066 --> 00:10:38,037
could you escort him to his room?

184
00:10:38,104 --> 00:10:39,038
Yes sir.

185
00:10:39,105 --> 00:10:40,272
Sir, let me...

186
00:10:40,339 --> 00:10:43,409
- Mr. Kanemoto, Please come this way.
- Thank you for your time.

187
00:10:43,476 --> 00:10:44,510
Thank you as well.

188
00:10:44,910 --> 00:10:45,745
This way please.

189
00:10:51,717 --> 00:10:52,718
What's wrong?

190
00:10:52,785 --> 00:10:54,720
It's this week's tabloid news.

191
00:10:56,856 --> 00:10:57,957
KANEMOTO'S DISAPPEARING FUNDS

192
00:10:58,024 --> 00:10:58,958
AND HIS SUSPICIOUS BLACK SHADOW!

193
00:10:59,025 --> 00:11:01,293
Mr. Kanemoto's scandal has been exposed.

194
00:11:02,962 --> 00:11:05,598
It is possible that
this hospitalisation for routine tests

195
00:11:05,665 --> 00:11:07,333
is his excuse to hide.

196
00:11:09,035 --> 00:11:13,272
I'm not sure if it's a good time...
to accept his hospitalisation.

197
00:11:13,339 --> 00:11:14,306
What should we do?

198
00:11:15,641 --> 00:11:19,111
I already told him that
he can stay here...

199
00:11:20,279 --> 00:11:21,747
as long as he'd like.

200
00:11:22,815 --> 00:11:23,849
Goodness.

201
00:11:28,054 --> 00:11:31,323
Kikawada, you heard, right?

202
00:11:31,857 --> 00:11:32,692
No, sir.

203
00:11:34,126 --> 00:11:35,027
You did.

204
00:11:36,562 --> 00:11:37,396
No, sir.

205
00:11:43,035 --> 00:11:44,837
I came to Tokyo,

206
00:11:45,404 --> 00:11:48,274
to make my way to the top...
in this hierarchical pyramid!

207
00:11:54,547 --> 00:11:55,981
Is it that bad?

208
00:11:57,183 --> 00:11:58,317
Sure is.

209
00:11:59,085 --> 00:12:01,921
Multi-centric colon cancer, Stage three B.

210
00:12:02,688 --> 00:12:03,656
Oh, my goodness.

211
00:12:04,657 --> 00:12:06,025
How old are you?

212
00:12:06,759 --> 00:12:07,626
80.

213
00:12:08,594 --> 00:12:10,930
80?

214
00:12:12,798 --> 00:12:15,534
Okay, let's run a few more tests.

215
00:12:16,068 --> 00:12:18,104
Laparoscopic surgery is less taxing
to your body.

216
00:12:18,804 --> 00:12:20,039
- No way.
- Huh?

217
00:12:20,106 --> 00:12:21,941
- I'm going home.
- Dear!

218
00:12:22,007 --> 00:12:23,943
Without the treatment, you're gonna die.

219
00:12:24,009 --> 00:12:26,679
If that is my fate, so be it.

220
00:12:27,913 --> 00:12:30,182
- Let's go home.
- Wait.

221
00:12:30,883 --> 00:12:32,485
Please wait right there.

222
00:12:33,319 --> 00:12:35,821
Dr. Daimon, can you remove this cancer?

223
00:12:35,888 --> 00:12:37,022
Yes, why?

224
00:12:37,089 --> 00:12:38,290
Then it's decided.

225
00:12:38,858 --> 00:12:43,462
If Dr. Daimon takes the charge of your
surgery, it is certain to be a success.

226
00:12:44,363 --> 00:12:47,199
Let's get you admitted
and begin the treatment.

227
00:12:47,833 --> 00:12:48,734
Really?

228
00:12:48,801 --> 00:12:49,969
Wait a minute.

229
00:12:50,302 --> 00:12:53,706
I didn't say I'm getting admitted.
I said I'm going home.

230
00:12:54,206 --> 00:12:58,477
You are the village chief
of Nijikawamura, right?

231
00:13:01,213 --> 00:13:05,584
"Nijikawamura leads in the first place of
the happiest villages in Japan,"

232
00:13:05,651 --> 00:13:08,621
"It's managed by
the poorest village chief."

233
00:13:08,687 --> 00:13:11,457
I didn't want the title at all.

234
00:13:11,924 --> 00:13:15,494
I just worked hard for the villagers,
and it turned out that way.

235
00:13:15,561 --> 00:13:16,695
That's all.

236
00:13:17,129 --> 00:13:18,697
Splendid.

237
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:22,101
Let's get started on the formal
procedures right away.

238
00:13:22,802 --> 00:13:24,003
Thank you.

239
00:13:24,069 --> 00:13:26,005
It's not your decision to make!

240
00:13:26,071 --> 00:13:27,573
There's no need to worry.

241
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:30,543
In your condition, I don't think...

242
00:13:30,943 --> 00:13:33,479
you would be comfortable in a deluxe room,

243
00:13:33,546 --> 00:13:35,714
so I will show you to
the general ward for you.

244
00:13:35,781 --> 00:13:38,317
That's not what I meant.

245
00:13:38,384 --> 00:13:41,320
I won't be hospitalised. Never.

246
00:13:41,387 --> 00:13:44,190
Hey, are you afraid of the operation?

247
00:13:46,025 --> 00:13:47,126
I'm not afraid!

248
00:13:48,460 --> 00:13:51,230
They kindly offered you
the best treatment.

249
00:13:54,166 --> 00:13:56,068
PRIVATE ROOM A

250
00:13:58,504 --> 00:13:59,338
Come in.

251
00:14:00,072 --> 00:14:02,508
- Please excuse us.
- Excuse me.

252
00:14:03,108 --> 00:14:06,111
This is a pretty nice room! I'm liking it.

253
00:14:06,745 --> 00:14:10,049
- Mr. Kanemoto, the thing is...
- I'm going to display this right here.

254
00:14:10,616 --> 00:14:12,718
I got it from an online auction.

255
00:14:12,785 --> 00:14:15,454
It fetched a higher price than I expected,

256
00:14:15,521 --> 00:14:17,590
I worked so hard to win this.

257
00:14:17,656 --> 00:14:21,160
Auction, really...
It didn't come out of the political funds.

258
00:14:26,565 --> 00:14:28,968
Why of course, we know that.

259
00:14:31,804 --> 00:14:36,709
- So what brought you here?
- Well, there was a small mistake.

260
00:14:36,775 --> 00:14:37,810
A mistake?

261
00:14:39,678 --> 00:14:41,714
- The reason of the mistake.
- Well...

262
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:47,486
This room was scheduled to be
renovated starting this evening.

263
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:50,322
Are you saying I should
move to another room?

264
00:14:51,657 --> 00:14:56,829
No, actually, the private rooms are full.

265
00:14:56,896 --> 00:14:59,098
- Full?
- Please don't worry.

266
00:14:59,164 --> 00:15:03,335
We have arranged a private room
at our Satellite hospital for you.

267
00:15:04,436 --> 00:15:07,439
- Are you telling me to get out?
- We are terribly sorry!

268
00:15:07,506 --> 00:15:08,674
We are terribly sorry!

269
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:12,511
I won't leave!
Even a large group room is fine!

270
00:15:12,578 --> 00:15:14,513
I am staying at this hospital!

271
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:16,348
Doctor! Doctor!

272
00:15:16,415 --> 00:15:18,884
- You accepted the money, right?
- Yes sir!

273
00:15:18,951 --> 00:15:19,952
Why did you admit it?

274
00:15:23,756 --> 00:15:24,823
You said it.

275
00:15:26,492 --> 00:15:28,227
You definitely said "Yes sir".

276
00:15:28,294 --> 00:15:32,431
I am Toko Kubo, the Deputy Director
of Toutei University Hospital.

277
00:15:33,132 --> 00:15:35,801
I have an announcement to make today.

278
00:15:36,135 --> 00:15:42,641
The village Chief,
Hideo Nioka, of Nijikawamura...

279
00:15:42,708 --> 00:15:46,845
which had selected as the happiest town
stayed in our hospital today.

280
00:15:49,381 --> 00:15:51,817
He is the poorest headman in the country.

281
00:15:51,884 --> 00:15:56,655
We here at Toutei University Hospital.

282
00:15:57,056 --> 00:15:59,091
Promise to save Chief Nioka's life.

283
00:16:00,859 --> 00:16:02,761
- That's good news.
- Unbelievable.

284
00:16:09,868 --> 00:16:12,471
- Stop.
- Please stay still.

285
00:16:14,206 --> 00:16:15,040
It's bad!

286
00:16:15,107 --> 00:16:18,143
Yes? What is this fuss about?

287
00:16:18,210 --> 00:16:20,479
Ku...

288
00:16:20,546 --> 00:16:23,615
What's with all this cooing.
Are you a pigeon!

289
00:16:23,682 --> 00:16:25,417
Ku? So what's...

290
00:16:25,884 --> 00:16:29,088
Deputy Director has called a conference.

291
00:16:30,055 --> 00:16:31,090
A conference?

292
00:16:33,659 --> 00:16:36,428
There is a rumour
that congressman Kanemoto...

293
00:16:36,495 --> 00:16:39,865
who allegedly misappropriated his funds,
was admitted here today. Is it true?

294
00:16:39,932 --> 00:16:41,633
What illness does he have?

295
00:16:41,700 --> 00:16:42,901
Isn't he feigning his illness?

296
00:16:42,968 --> 00:16:45,137
Is this hospital
a hideout for politicians?

297
00:16:45,204 --> 00:16:47,873
- What do you have to say?
- This can be a serious problem.

298
00:16:47,940 --> 00:16:49,008
This topic...

299
00:16:50,142 --> 00:16:54,380
is under Director Hiruma's care therefore
I have nothing to say at all.

300
00:16:54,446 --> 00:16:57,649
The conference is over. Please leave.

301
00:16:57,716 --> 00:16:59,218
Please tell us something.

302
00:16:59,284 --> 00:17:01,887
If you're so interested, ask the director!

303
00:17:03,822 --> 00:17:06,091
We are finished. Thank you.

304
00:17:06,458 --> 00:17:07,826
Please leave now.

305
00:17:08,327 --> 00:17:10,262
Thank you very much.

306
00:17:10,696 --> 00:17:13,532
What does she think she's doing now?

307
00:17:14,333 --> 00:17:16,201
- Kikawada,
- Yes, sir.

308
00:17:17,369 --> 00:17:23,041
Don't you think this
wouldn't have happened...

309
00:17:23,108 --> 00:17:25,010
if you hadn't fail to kick out

310
00:17:25,411 --> 00:17:27,746
this crooked congressman
from our hospital?

311
00:17:27,813 --> 00:17:29,248
I am terribly sorry.

312
00:17:30,916 --> 00:17:32,351
- Director,
- Yes?

313
00:17:33,986 --> 00:17:36,855
I can make him leave.

314
00:17:37,856 --> 00:17:40,025
- What are you talking about?
- You can?

315
00:17:40,092 --> 00:17:43,695
We should preform tests on
Kanemoto right away.

316
00:17:44,830 --> 00:17:47,933
If it is a feigned disease,

317
00:17:48,367 --> 00:17:51,470
then we have no moral reason
to allow him to stay.

318
00:17:51,537 --> 00:17:55,407
That's true. That's it.
Let's move forward with that.

319
00:17:57,876 --> 00:17:58,844
Yes sir.

320
00:17:59,745 --> 00:18:00,879
Thank you.

321
00:18:12,224 --> 00:18:13,992
- Kikawada.
- Yes, sir.

322
00:18:15,727 --> 00:18:17,096
You're still here?

323
00:18:19,665 --> 00:18:21,767
Would you like to get fired?

324
00:18:22,634 --> 00:18:23,502
No, sir.

325
00:18:23,569 --> 00:18:24,703
Then,

326
00:18:25,137 --> 00:18:30,342
the treatment of Mayor Nioka
the man of high integrity,

327
00:18:31,610 --> 00:18:36,515
to take care of him at Internal Medicine.

328
00:18:36,582 --> 00:18:37,850
- Yes, sir.
- I...

329
00:18:38,350 --> 00:18:41,820
won't let that wicked old lady Kubo
do whatever she pleases!

330
00:18:41,887 --> 00:18:43,055
Yes sir.

331
00:18:43,122 --> 00:18:44,890
Wait.

332
00:18:45,457 --> 00:18:46,625
About your "Yes sir."

333
00:18:48,127 --> 00:18:50,295
Try it like this. Do you get it?

334
00:18:50,362 --> 00:18:51,730
Yes sir.

335
00:18:52,764 --> 00:18:54,900
Hey! Spin it when you do it.

336
00:18:54,967 --> 00:18:55,934
Yes sir.

337
00:18:56,001 --> 00:18:57,469
Please excuse me.

338
00:18:57,536 --> 00:18:58,971
Don't you jump off the roof!

339
00:18:59,738 --> 00:19:00,572
Hey!

340
00:19:02,407 --> 00:19:03,876
What's he got to mope about, seriously.

341
00:19:07,379 --> 00:19:09,648
PATIENT: HIDEO NIOKA MALE, 80 YEARS OLD

342
00:19:11,216 --> 00:19:12,050
Hey, Daimon.

343
00:19:12,584 --> 00:19:15,521
I heard you're going to
perform Nioka's operation?

344
00:19:17,656 --> 00:19:20,359
The Deputy Director really
boasted about you.

345
00:19:20,425 --> 00:19:22,227
You just can't fail, you know?

346
00:19:23,595 --> 00:19:26,498
"I never fail." Right? I heard you.

347
00:19:28,367 --> 00:19:31,570
The bigger problem,
is the dark public figure.

348
00:19:31,637 --> 00:19:33,805
Kanemoto is no good.

349
00:19:33,872 --> 00:19:38,343
I know. He's been going to hot spring
in Hakone every weekend with his lover.

350
00:19:39,978 --> 00:19:42,848
- Hakone?
- He had meetings in a private room.

351
00:19:42,915 --> 00:19:44,716
With an outdoor hot-spring bath.

352
00:19:45,484 --> 00:19:46,919
Outdoor hot-spring?

353
00:19:50,255 --> 00:19:52,124
KANEMOTO HOLDS MEETINGS
IN A PRIVATE ROOM WITH HIS LOVER

354
00:19:56,495 --> 00:19:58,197
Let me down.

355
00:19:58,263 --> 00:20:01,066
I don't have time to waste at a hospital!

356
00:20:01,133 --> 00:20:04,002
We understand your feelings,

357
00:20:04,069 --> 00:20:06,138
but please focus on your treatment!

358
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:08,073
That's what our villagers want!

359
00:20:08,140 --> 00:20:10,709
Chief, please get the surgery.

360
00:20:11,043 --> 00:20:15,280
See? you have so many people
worrying about you.

361
00:20:15,347 --> 00:20:16,815
You have to get well soon.

362
00:20:16,882 --> 00:20:19,184
But I haven't consented
to the surgery yet!

363
00:20:19,251 --> 00:20:21,253
If you don't get the operation,
you will die.

364
00:20:21,320 --> 00:20:22,754
- I don't care!
- Dear!

365
00:20:24,189 --> 00:20:26,225
You can't be stubborn like this anymore.

366
00:20:26,592 --> 00:20:28,360
Do not ever say such things again!

367
00:20:32,130 --> 00:20:34,633
You're scarier than I thought.

368
00:20:35,934 --> 00:20:36,768
Let's go.

369
00:20:41,607 --> 00:20:43,342
MR. K

370
00:20:43,408 --> 00:20:44,276
Goodness.

371
00:20:45,444 --> 00:20:46,345
All right.

372
00:20:48,847 --> 00:20:49,915
Oh. There's Hakone.

373
00:20:50,616 --> 00:20:51,750
What are you doing here?

374
00:20:52,117 --> 00:20:55,087
Are private rooms with open-air
baths expensive?

375
00:20:55,153 --> 00:20:58,957
I said I would stay in a common room,
but it doesn't mean I would share!

376
00:20:59,024 --> 00:21:01,560
Are the hot-spring eggs
really black like this?

377
00:21:01,627 --> 00:21:03,228
Get off!

378
00:21:03,295 --> 00:21:05,197
Call the director!

379
00:21:05,264 --> 00:21:08,634
Aren't you too old to
lose temper so easily?

380
00:21:08,700 --> 00:21:10,269
You are so narrow-minded.

381
00:21:11,770 --> 00:21:12,638
What?

382
00:21:12,704 --> 00:21:15,240
Don't forget that you're in a hospital.

383
00:21:16,074 --> 00:21:19,011
A good person would never
lose his temper here.

384
00:21:19,544 --> 00:21:23,081
- It only brings out bad repercussions.
- That's right.

385
00:21:23,148 --> 00:21:26,618
After all you end up shortening
your own lifespan.

386
00:21:27,286 --> 00:21:30,255
That's our mayor! Nothing is gained
from losing your temper.

387
00:21:30,322 --> 00:21:31,323
Exactly.

388
00:21:32,591 --> 00:21:34,693
I apologise. He is always like this.

389
00:21:35,193 --> 00:21:37,629
But he doesn't mean to offend anyone.

390
00:21:39,464 --> 00:21:41,800
Please, treat us kindly.

391
00:21:43,335 --> 00:21:45,704
Then I guess you two
will be fine to share a room.

392
00:21:51,610 --> 00:21:54,179
Putting the poorest chief
in the country...

393
00:21:54,246 --> 00:21:56,315
in the same room as the congressman

394
00:21:56,381 --> 00:21:58,817
involved in the most
money related scandals

395
00:21:58,884 --> 00:22:00,819
is quite an interesting combination.

396
00:22:00,886 --> 00:22:03,355
The congressman must just
have a feigned illness, right?

397
00:22:03,689 --> 00:22:06,058
The main concern is the mayor, though.

398
00:22:06,124 --> 00:22:08,460
We don't know if he can take
an operation at his age.

399
00:22:09,027 --> 00:22:12,798
At that age, post-operation
risks are high,

400
00:22:12,864 --> 00:22:15,500
and his body may not
handle a long surgery.

401
00:22:15,567 --> 00:22:18,904
That won't be a problem for me.
I work fast.

402
00:22:18,970 --> 00:22:23,909
And, I'm also quick at
getting one step toward winning!

403
00:22:27,145 --> 00:22:28,380
Excuse me.

404
00:22:29,681 --> 00:22:32,718
Is this the residence of
Dr. Michiko Daimon?

405
00:22:32,784 --> 00:22:33,785
May I ask who you are?

406
00:22:33,852 --> 00:22:35,354
He's from that Gramps' village.

407
00:22:35,420 --> 00:22:38,890
My name is Osaki,
and I am the chief's official assistant.

408
00:22:38,957 --> 00:22:43,695
Thank you very much
for taking care of the chief.

409
00:22:43,762 --> 00:22:44,796
Oh, not at all.

410
00:22:44,863 --> 00:22:48,767
Thank you for asking
our Daimon for your case.

411
00:22:49,234 --> 00:22:53,205
I'm here to deliver a gift from villagers.

412
00:22:53,739 --> 00:22:54,573
A gift?

413
00:22:55,240 --> 00:22:56,875
It's nothing special.

414
00:23:07,719 --> 00:23:10,222
Please come in.

415
00:23:10,288 --> 00:23:11,289
Thank you. Excuse me.

416
00:23:13,392 --> 00:23:16,962
Although the chief can be quite
stubborn at times,

417
00:23:17,028 --> 00:23:19,431
he is a great man
who you can really respect.

418
00:23:19,498 --> 00:23:22,367
The villagers really want him
to make a full recovery.

419
00:23:22,434 --> 00:23:24,936
This is a token of our sincere gratitude.

420
00:23:27,105 --> 00:23:28,507
Please accept this.

421
00:23:29,040 --> 00:23:30,142
I will.

422
00:23:32,544 --> 00:23:33,845
Please excuse me.

423
00:23:38,383 --> 00:23:39,251
Goodbye.

424
00:23:42,187 --> 00:23:44,022
It's pretty thick.

425
00:23:44,089 --> 00:23:48,894
- Isn't he the poorest chief in Japan?
- I'm not sure if you should take this.

426
00:23:49,461 --> 00:23:50,495
Wait!

427
00:23:51,163 --> 00:23:52,297
It's heavy.

428
00:23:52,364 --> 00:23:55,434
That's not fair, Akira. That is for me.

429
00:23:55,500 --> 00:23:56,368
How much is it?

430
00:23:56,435 --> 00:23:59,404
You guys are so greedy.

431
00:23:59,471 --> 00:24:00,572
Show me.

432
00:24:00,906 --> 00:24:02,574
- Just a little.
- Fine.

433
00:24:11,149 --> 00:24:13,552
PRE-OPERATIVE CONFERNCE

434
00:24:13,618 --> 00:24:16,188
We will now begin this week's conference.

435
00:24:16,655 --> 00:24:19,691
The first case is Hideo Nioka. Age of 80.

436
00:24:19,758 --> 00:24:23,061
He's diagnosed with
Stage three B colon cancer.

437
00:24:24,062 --> 00:24:27,666
I will be removing it. He is my patient.

438
00:24:28,400 --> 00:24:29,367
You can't.

439
00:24:29,935 --> 00:24:33,038
- Why not?
- He is an important patient

440
00:24:33,104 --> 00:24:34,706
as he's popular around the nation.

441
00:24:35,240 --> 00:24:37,709
We cannot leave him to a freelancer
surgeon like you.

442
00:24:39,110 --> 00:24:39,945
- Yes sir.
- Yes sir.

443
00:24:41,580 --> 00:24:44,316
Aren't you the one that
turned him away at first?

444
00:24:44,382 --> 00:24:45,884
The situation has changed.

445
00:24:46,585 --> 00:24:48,987
This is Director Hiruma's wish as well.

446
00:24:50,021 --> 00:24:51,156
Yes sir.

447
00:24:51,590 --> 00:24:53,191
That's ridiculous.

448
00:24:53,258 --> 00:24:56,628
He has one tumour in his colon,

449
00:24:56,695 --> 00:24:58,363
and two in his rectum.

450
00:24:59,631 --> 00:25:01,766
It is dangerous to remove
all of them at once.

451
00:25:03,101 --> 00:25:06,905
The best treatment would be
a combination of LV and bevacizumab

452
00:25:06,972 --> 00:25:08,573
along with chemotherapy.

453
00:25:24,523 --> 00:25:25,357
What is it?

454
00:25:25,957 --> 00:25:29,261
If you are going to be in charge of
this case, I'll give it to you.

455
00:25:29,694 --> 00:25:30,629
What?

456
00:25:30,695 --> 00:25:32,197
Gratuity from Gramps.

457
00:25:34,733 --> 00:25:37,302
Daimon, you received this?

458
00:25:38,169 --> 00:25:40,405
How shameless can you be.

459
00:25:41,606 --> 00:25:42,574
You don't need it?

460
00:25:42,641 --> 00:25:43,842
Of course not!

461
00:25:43,909 --> 00:25:44,910
I see.

462
00:25:45,577 --> 00:25:49,648
I will return this properly.
Never receive such thing again!

463
00:25:49,714 --> 00:25:51,349
- Compliance!
- Yes, sir.

464
00:25:54,286 --> 00:25:56,154
Well then, I'll leave it to you.

465
00:26:06,131 --> 00:26:09,467
Dr. Saionji, Kanemoto's
test results are ready.

466
00:26:10,569 --> 00:26:12,704
Great, get ready to discharge him.

467
00:26:12,771 --> 00:26:15,040
Well, actually...

468
00:26:26,484 --> 00:26:28,053
Colorectal cancer stage four.

469
00:26:30,255 --> 00:26:31,923
The cancer has not only
spread to the liver,

470
00:26:31,990 --> 00:26:34,626
but there are also tumours
in three other organs.

471
00:26:34,693 --> 00:26:37,796
Synchronous multiple metastatic
colorectal cancer.

472
00:26:37,862 --> 00:26:40,832
It seems the situation has become
pretty difficult, Dr. Saionji.

473
00:26:41,466 --> 00:26:44,069
It turns out you weren't thinking enough

474
00:26:44,135 --> 00:26:46,271
when you framed me.

475
00:26:47,606 --> 00:26:48,473
Hey,

476
00:26:50,575 --> 00:26:52,444
What do you mean by framing?

477
00:26:52,510 --> 00:26:54,646
He shouldn't have been tested!

478
00:26:55,046 --> 00:26:56,047
This is your mistake.

479
00:26:56,815 --> 00:26:57,849
Mistake?

480
00:26:57,916 --> 00:27:02,487
Hey, Just do the surgery.

481
00:27:03,121 --> 00:27:04,289
I will do it.

482
00:27:04,856 --> 00:27:07,859
Even if you do cure him,
there is no benefit to us.

483
00:27:07,926 --> 00:27:10,061
It is rather damaging
to our hospital brand.

484
00:27:10,128 --> 00:27:12,998
You were called here
for the sake of the reputation.

485
00:27:13,064 --> 00:27:18,703
- I can't allow you to take charge of him.
- So you just throw sick people out?

486
00:27:18,770 --> 00:27:21,539
All right then, you, part-timer.
Do the operation.

487
00:27:21,606 --> 00:27:22,440
Yes sir.

488
00:27:22,507 --> 00:27:24,809
He's putting a lot of pressure
to the Surgical Department.

489
00:27:24,876 --> 00:27:27,278
It is surely a payback.

490
00:27:27,345 --> 00:27:30,982
Internal Medicine Dept. will concentrate
on Japan's treasure, Mayor Nioka.

491
00:27:31,383 --> 00:27:34,786
Dr. Saionji, wish you luck.

492
00:27:49,768 --> 00:27:51,136
Go on ahead of me.

493
00:27:51,202 --> 00:27:52,037
Yes sir.

494
00:28:04,816 --> 00:28:06,851
I wonder how much it is.

495
00:28:14,693 --> 00:28:15,827
This is...

496
00:28:21,299 --> 00:28:22,834
"Nijikawamura village hall."

497
00:28:23,368 --> 00:28:26,471
"10 percent off all items
at the Autumn vegetable festival."

498
00:28:26,538 --> 00:28:27,806
It's healthy, isn't it?

499
00:28:34,713 --> 00:28:35,547
Cancer?

500
00:28:36,981 --> 00:28:37,916
Cancer?

501
00:28:38,683 --> 00:28:41,252
- Me?
- Colorectal cancer with liver metastasis.

502
00:28:41,786 --> 00:28:43,121
But you will be cured if we operate now.

503
00:28:45,523 --> 00:28:47,826
- You can cure it?
- If we operate.

504
00:28:47,892 --> 00:28:49,360
Who will operate?

505
00:28:49,828 --> 00:28:53,264
Besides me, no one wants
to take charge of it.

506
00:28:54,399 --> 00:28:56,768
- You are going to operate on me?
- Yes.

507
00:28:56,835 --> 00:28:58,570
But you're a part-timer!

508
00:28:59,270 --> 00:29:03,975
I'll pay as much as it takes!
Let me get treatment by another doctor.

509
00:29:05,543 --> 00:29:07,345
You may be luckier that you think.

510
00:29:07,412 --> 00:29:08,246
Huh?

511
00:29:09,180 --> 00:29:11,716
I never fail.

512
00:29:13,084 --> 00:29:13,918
What?

513
00:29:13,985 --> 00:29:17,756
From now on, we,
the Internal Medicine Department

514
00:29:17,822 --> 00:29:20,692
will be prepared to treat you perfectly.

515
00:29:21,092 --> 00:29:23,695
How long does he need to be hospitalised?

516
00:29:24,496 --> 00:29:27,999
Chemotherapy is a method
that takes patience...

517
00:29:28,366 --> 00:29:31,536
I suggest you think of it as a long shot.

518
00:29:31,603 --> 00:29:32,470
No!

519
00:29:33,238 --> 00:29:37,075
In the first place,
longer treatment will cost more.

520
00:29:38,843 --> 00:29:41,679
How much will it cost?

521
00:29:42,213 --> 00:29:43,581
It will be about this much.

522
00:29:43,648 --> 00:29:45,550
($11,598)

523
00:29:45,617 --> 00:29:49,454
I cannot afford this kind of money!

524
00:29:50,488 --> 00:29:55,360
This much money could pay several wells,
and fixing roads for the village.

525
00:29:56,227 --> 00:29:59,063
However, money cannot replace your life.

526
00:30:00,231 --> 00:30:03,635
Even if I have to sell this
black hair, I will raise the money.

527
00:30:03,701 --> 00:30:04,435
Black hair?

528
00:30:04,502 --> 00:30:10,975
I can never let you
cut your hair just for me. I won't do it!

529
00:30:11,042 --> 00:30:12,010
Honey.

530
00:30:15,480 --> 00:30:16,614
Excuse me.

531
00:30:18,516 --> 00:30:20,451
You do not need to worry about money.

532
00:30:20,518 --> 00:30:22,153
Deputy Director, I'm so sorry.

533
00:30:22,220 --> 00:30:24,455
This was the director's desire.

534
00:30:24,522 --> 00:30:26,024
Forget about that!

535
00:30:28,893 --> 00:30:33,131
It is this hospital's mission
to save Chief Nioka's life.

536
00:30:34,065 --> 00:30:37,869
The hospital will cover
the full charge of the treatment.

537
00:30:39,571 --> 00:30:43,408
The people all around the nation
are wishing for your safe recovery.

538
00:30:46,077 --> 00:30:48,179
PRAY FOR CHIEF NIOKA!
A LIGHT OF HOPE FOR NIOKA!

539
00:30:48,246 --> 00:30:50,782
NIOKA IS POOR, BUT IMPORTANT
JAPAN SHOULD CARE FOR HIM MORE.

540
00:30:52,217 --> 00:30:53,885
This is wonderful.

541
00:30:54,385 --> 00:30:56,855
You're amazing, Deputy Director Kubo.

542
00:30:57,322 --> 00:31:00,191
You can receive all the treatment
you need with this.

543
00:31:00,258 --> 00:31:01,092
Honey.

544
00:31:02,093 --> 00:31:03,895
Is this all right with you, Mr. Nioka?

545
00:31:06,030 --> 00:31:07,365
Thank you very much!

546
00:31:08,600 --> 00:31:09,934
Thank you!

547
00:31:10,001 --> 00:31:11,669
Then it's decided.

548
00:31:11,736 --> 00:31:12,837
Yes!

549
00:31:12,904 --> 00:31:13,872
Please be at ease.

550
00:31:30,688 --> 00:31:31,623
Gramps!

551
00:31:33,558 --> 00:31:34,459
Hey!

552
00:31:34,525 --> 00:31:35,960
Gramps!

553
00:31:38,563 --> 00:31:40,665
Where are you going?

554
00:31:40,732 --> 00:31:42,767
Hey wait!

555
00:31:45,003 --> 00:31:45,837
Gramps!

556
00:31:48,706 --> 00:31:50,208
I'm okay.

557
00:31:50,808 --> 00:31:53,177
If you really don't do anything,
you will die.

558
00:31:54,879 --> 00:31:57,415
If I get the treatment,
I won't make it on time.

559
00:31:58,583 --> 00:32:00,018
Make on time?

560
00:32:00,418 --> 00:32:03,621
There are things I have to do.

561
00:32:04,155 --> 00:32:05,890
There are people waiting for me.

562
00:32:06,758 --> 00:32:07,926
People waiting?

563
00:32:09,761 --> 00:32:10,795
The villagers?

564
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:18,836
I don't really know
about complicated matters,

565
00:32:19,637 --> 00:32:23,808
but the world could can manage to
go around without you. Don't you think?

566
00:32:26,477 --> 00:32:29,414
Will I be able... to survive?

567
00:32:31,916 --> 00:32:35,253
Will you listen to my last wish?

568
00:32:41,993 --> 00:32:44,762
HIDEO NIOKA MR. K

569
00:32:57,342 --> 00:32:59,210
You have cancer?

570
00:33:03,715 --> 00:33:07,018
They told me I do too.

571
00:33:10,154 --> 00:33:15,026
This is a pain.

572
00:33:15,827 --> 00:33:17,328
I'm sure anyone would flounder

573
00:33:18,262 --> 00:33:21,799
if told they have cancer. It's natural.

574
00:33:23,067 --> 00:33:24,335
It's OK.

575
00:33:25,403 --> 00:33:30,675
One time, I used to be called the
No.1 candidate for prime minister.

576
00:33:31,509 --> 00:33:33,978
I guess I got caught up in the image.

577
00:33:34,846 --> 00:33:38,950
Before I knew it, I was going to Hakone
every week with my lover.

578
00:33:39,584 --> 00:33:41,386
Those eggs were too delicious.

579
00:33:42,253 --> 00:33:46,090
So what's the deal?
I did spend political funds to taste them.

580
00:33:46,557 --> 00:33:49,794
It's impossible to be exposed
to the public 24 hours a day.

581
00:33:50,595 --> 00:33:51,996
What's so wrong about me?

582
00:33:52,663 --> 00:33:57,368
Politicians must be considerate
of the people's feelings.

583
00:33:59,303 --> 00:34:02,874
You're getting criticized because
you only cared about your mistress.

584
00:34:04,042 --> 00:34:06,744
It's like a punishment.

585
00:34:07,178 --> 00:34:09,981
Well, everything is exposed after all.

586
00:34:11,115 --> 00:34:15,486
The only thing you can do is to get down
on your knees and apologise to the people.

587
00:34:16,988 --> 00:34:20,591
It's best to apologise
right after bad behavior.

588
00:34:21,325 --> 00:34:22,827
You can't make lame excuses.

589
00:34:25,897 --> 00:34:29,867
If you do, it'll only rub
people the wrong way.

590
00:34:32,670 --> 00:34:35,440
Do you think I'll be able to survive?

591
00:34:36,741 --> 00:34:38,643
That I don't know.

592
00:34:40,244 --> 00:34:41,112
I don't know.

593
00:34:43,147 --> 00:34:44,282
However,

594
00:34:47,652 --> 00:34:49,720
without us

595
00:34:51,422 --> 00:34:54,792
the world will manage to go around.

596
00:35:14,312 --> 00:35:15,379
Good work today.

597
00:35:15,446 --> 00:35:16,447
Good work.

598
00:35:16,881 --> 00:35:17,949
Chief Kikawada!

599
00:35:20,351 --> 00:35:22,720
- Hey, this is a hospital. Don't run.
- I apologise,

600
00:35:22,787 --> 00:35:25,389
but Dr. Daimon has started
Mayor Nioka's surgery.

601
00:35:25,456 --> 00:35:26,190
What?

602
00:35:26,757 --> 00:35:28,659
He's running!

603
00:35:38,202 --> 00:35:41,038
COLORECTAL CANCER REMOVAL SURGERY
PATIENT: HIDEO NIOKA

604
00:35:42,974 --> 00:35:45,877
- First Assistant, pull the mesentery.
- Got it.

605
00:35:47,044 --> 00:35:50,014
Is it okay to perform
this operation without permission?

606
00:35:50,081 --> 00:35:53,317
- Stop chattering and move your hands.
- Fine.

607
00:35:53,384 --> 00:35:55,286
You can't operate if you tap...

608
00:35:55,353 --> 00:35:57,121
There's the chattering again.

609
00:35:57,188 --> 00:36:01,092
That Internal Medicine Chief
will definitely be here anytime.

610
00:36:01,826 --> 00:36:02,994
See, here he is.

611
00:36:06,597 --> 00:36:08,799
Why are you operating?

612
00:36:09,800 --> 00:36:12,069
He is my patient.
Please stop her immediately.

613
00:36:12,136 --> 00:36:15,139
There is nothing we can do
if it's the patients wish.

614
00:36:15,773 --> 00:36:17,341
There is a letter of consent.

615
00:36:20,011 --> 00:36:21,345
LETTER OF CONSENT

616
00:36:21,946 --> 00:36:24,148
A letter of consent? Why?

617
00:36:24,215 --> 00:36:27,118
Who cares as long as he's cured.

618
00:36:27,185 --> 00:36:28,920
If this heals him completely,

619
00:36:29,287 --> 00:36:31,222
there is a big advantage for the hospital.

620
00:36:32,356 --> 00:36:35,459
I don't think he can handle
the surgery at that age!

621
00:36:36,160 --> 00:36:37,528
Hey, Daimon! Stop it!

622
00:36:37,995 --> 00:36:39,864
Do you want to kill the patient?

623
00:36:39,931 --> 00:36:40,998
I decline.

624
00:36:41,732 --> 00:36:44,835
That's why I'm telling you not to operate.

625
00:36:45,269 --> 00:36:46,137
Don't do it!

626
00:36:49,440 --> 00:36:50,474
Daimon!

627
00:36:51,442 --> 00:36:52,610
Look at me!

628
00:36:53,578 --> 00:36:56,080
OPERATING TIME: 3 HOURS

629
00:37:12,463 --> 00:37:15,533
Removal of the lymph node
and intestine wall completed.

630
00:37:15,600 --> 00:37:17,335
You're as fast as usual.

631
00:37:17,401 --> 00:37:19,403
- His vitals are stable.
- What's next?

632
00:37:19,470 --> 00:37:21,072
- We're finished.
- What?

633
00:37:21,906 --> 00:37:25,476
- There are still two left!
- I'll leave the suture to you.

634
00:37:26,410 --> 00:37:27,612
What are you doing?

635
00:37:27,678 --> 00:37:31,349
Don't you dare stop!
Finish the surgery properly!

636
00:37:34,352 --> 00:37:36,454
You'll make it on time, Gramps.

637
00:37:39,757 --> 00:37:40,725
Hey Demon!

638
00:37:41,993 --> 00:37:43,261
What is going on...

639
00:37:44,929 --> 00:37:46,731
God!

640
00:37:47,632 --> 00:37:50,568
The surgery was too difficult
she threw it away! I knew it!

641
00:37:51,369 --> 00:37:54,438
That's why I said irresponsible
part-timers are no good!

642
00:37:54,505 --> 00:37:56,474
She couldn't remove them all?

643
00:37:57,341 --> 00:37:59,310
The operation was a failure.

644
00:38:03,281 --> 00:38:05,850
Michiko Daimon!

645
00:38:15,559 --> 00:38:18,095
Daimon! Why did you stop?

646
00:38:18,162 --> 00:38:19,964
Did she mess up the operation?

647
00:38:21,832 --> 00:38:24,568
It's five o'clock so I'm going home!

648
00:38:25,503 --> 00:38:28,539
Did you stopped
the operation because it's time?

649
00:38:48,292 --> 00:38:49,794
Nice work today.

650
00:38:52,029 --> 00:38:53,564
Oh, so you can talk.

651
00:39:04,308 --> 00:39:08,245
MICHIKO DAIMON

652
00:39:20,624 --> 00:39:22,259
Mayor Nioka's condition is stable.

653
00:39:23,294 --> 00:39:27,231
But Dr. Daimon left two tumours,
didn't she?

654
00:39:27,932 --> 00:39:30,000
The operation was said to be a failure.

655
00:39:33,871 --> 00:39:35,906
Call the Chief Surgeon immediately!

656
00:39:41,078 --> 00:39:42,580
About Kanemoto's operation,

657
00:39:43,347 --> 00:39:46,784
Daimon, you will no longer preform it.

658
00:39:46,851 --> 00:39:47,985
Why?

659
00:39:48,052 --> 00:39:50,921
Kanemoto said,
if you were to perform the surgery,

660
00:39:50,988 --> 00:39:52,556
he will not sign the consent.

661
00:39:53,357 --> 00:39:56,460
You know the reason, don't you?

662
00:39:59,196 --> 00:40:00,431
The new surgeon will be...

663
00:40:04,435 --> 00:40:06,871
Kitano.

664
00:40:10,441 --> 00:40:13,611
I'm counting on you.
Whether he's black or grey...

665
00:40:17,481 --> 00:40:18,549
a patient is a patient.

666
00:40:18,616 --> 00:40:21,085
Here comes the theatre.

667
00:40:21,952 --> 00:40:24,121
Kitano, will you take it?

668
00:40:26,157 --> 00:40:27,024
Of course.

669
00:40:27,691 --> 00:40:28,893
Can you do it?

670
00:40:30,027 --> 00:40:32,797
I will never leave tumours like you did.

671
00:40:32,863 --> 00:40:36,534
I will take them all out and leave
the area completely tumour-free.

672
00:40:37,701 --> 00:40:40,905
- Would you like me to assist?
- No, thank you.

673
00:40:42,006 --> 00:40:42,840
Oh really.

674
00:40:43,974 --> 00:40:46,210
Well, if you think
you can do it, go ahead.

675
00:40:51,816 --> 00:40:55,152
Not even in America can you find a
hard-headed female doctor like her.

676
00:40:55,219 --> 00:40:56,053
Kitano,

677
00:40:57,922 --> 00:41:00,558
- I'm counting on you...
- Leave it to me.

678
00:41:10,901 --> 00:41:12,203
Okay guys,

679
00:41:12,269 --> 00:41:16,874
we will now begin the partial colectomy,
along with a partial hepatectomy.

680
00:41:16,941 --> 00:41:19,376
- I look forward to working with you.
- As do we.

681
00:41:19,443 --> 00:41:22,680
Blood pressure and heart rate are normal.

682
00:41:22,746 --> 00:41:24,181
- Scalpel.
- Here.

683
00:41:26,417 --> 00:41:27,618
Incision.

684
00:41:36,393 --> 00:41:37,461
- Seer.
- Here.

685
00:41:51,709 --> 00:41:52,776
- Clamp.
- Here.

686
00:42:18,469 --> 00:42:19,570
Wonderful.

687
00:42:20,404 --> 00:42:23,807
What a dynamic and
splendid operation it is.

688
00:42:31,015 --> 00:42:32,283
- Drill.
- Here.

689
00:42:42,393 --> 00:42:45,829
Removal of S7 tumor completed.
One more to go.

690
00:42:45,896 --> 00:42:47,565
Moving on the removal of S4 tumor.

691
00:42:48,198 --> 00:42:49,266
Monopolar.

692
00:43:03,948 --> 00:43:04,782
Dr. Kitano.

693
00:43:05,182 --> 00:43:07,384
The tumor has spread to the liver canal.

694
00:43:07,451 --> 00:43:09,887
It is spread far more than I expected.

695
00:43:17,595 --> 00:43:20,097
Under that condition,
partial excision is impossible.

696
00:43:25,836 --> 00:43:29,239
I'm changing the procedure.
Cutting off the right hepatectomy.

697
00:43:33,577 --> 00:43:35,679
Kitano, it's inoperable. Close up!

698
00:43:35,746 --> 00:43:37,815
Don't go in any further. It's dangerous.

699
00:43:39,416 --> 00:43:41,318
Dr. Kitano, let's close.

700
00:43:41,385 --> 00:43:43,721
- Dr. Kitano!
- We are going to keep going.

701
00:44:01,105 --> 00:44:03,273
Detaching the interior vena cava.
Kelly's forceps.

702
00:44:13,417 --> 00:44:16,420
Wow. This may actually work.

703
00:44:22,960 --> 00:44:23,827
He got through it.

704
00:44:25,029 --> 00:44:27,831
He is indeed the world-famous Kitano.

705
00:44:42,746 --> 00:44:45,382
Bleeding from the portal vein.

706
00:44:47,651 --> 00:44:50,154
Blood pressure down to 70. Heart rate 100.

707
00:44:50,220 --> 00:44:51,188
This is bad.

708
00:44:51,255 --> 00:44:53,090
Suction. Sterilization gauze.

709
00:44:53,157 --> 00:44:54,658
- Prepare for transfusion.
- Yes.

710
00:45:03,734 --> 00:45:05,569
Dr. Kitano, it's still bleeding.

711
00:45:25,723 --> 00:45:26,557
Daimon!

712
00:45:28,959 --> 00:45:30,994
Just as I thought.

713
00:45:31,061 --> 00:45:33,397
That's why I asked if you could do it.

714
00:45:33,464 --> 00:45:35,332
Did you know the cancer was
progressing this far?

715
00:45:35,399 --> 00:45:37,501
You cut too much.

716
00:45:41,271 --> 00:45:42,272
Out of the way.

717
00:45:42,806 --> 00:45:43,907
Vitals?

718
00:45:43,974 --> 00:45:46,343
Blood pressure 63. Heart rate 122.

719
00:45:47,511 --> 00:45:48,479
Wait a minute!

720
00:45:48,979 --> 00:45:51,415
The S7 tumor hasn't been
completely removed either!

721
00:45:52,649 --> 00:45:54,351
What a sloppy work.

722
00:45:54,818 --> 00:45:55,786
- Clamp.
- Here.

723
00:46:03,293 --> 00:46:04,128
It stopped.

724
00:46:04,194 --> 00:46:05,095
Stop daydreaming

725
00:46:05,162 --> 00:46:06,563
and start suturing.

726
00:46:06,630 --> 00:46:08,766
Starting the central bisegmentectomy
of the liver.

727
00:46:08,832 --> 00:46:09,833
- Scalpel.
- Here.

728
00:46:20,511 --> 00:46:23,180
That's impossible!
Do you plan to fail again?

729
00:46:24,214 --> 00:46:25,582
I never fail.

730
00:46:25,649 --> 00:46:27,484
You already have, haven't you?

731
00:46:28,352 --> 00:46:29,953
I have never failed.

732
00:46:43,167 --> 00:46:44,601
You're so fast.

733
00:46:44,668 --> 00:46:46,403
- Move your hands.
- Okay.

734
00:46:55,312 --> 00:46:56,246
Beautiful.

735
00:46:58,182 --> 00:47:02,719
What a delicate
and truly beautiful operation.

736
00:47:22,139 --> 00:47:23,207
I'm finished.

737
00:47:23,273 --> 00:47:25,309
His vitals are 110 and 75.

738
00:47:34,184 --> 00:47:36,320
Go to Hakone with your own money, okay?

739
00:47:36,386 --> 00:47:38,488
- Nice work.
- Good work.

740
00:48:30,874 --> 00:48:33,477
The other day,

741
00:48:33,911 --> 00:48:38,682
Congressman Kanemoto was hospitalized for

742
00:48:38,749 --> 00:48:40,350
colorectal cancer liver metastasis.

743
00:48:40,417 --> 00:48:42,519
We are pleased to announce here,

744
00:48:42,920 --> 00:48:47,291
that his surgery was a success.

745
00:48:49,059 --> 00:48:51,028
Currently, Congressman Kanemoto...

746
00:48:51,094 --> 00:48:55,265
is the one currently
in the center of suspicions.

747
00:48:55,866 --> 00:48:57,868
For this reason,

748
00:48:57,935 --> 00:49:01,738
we did everything in our power...

749
00:49:01,805 --> 00:49:04,041
to cure his cancer.

750
00:49:04,107 --> 00:49:08,111
Congressman Kanemoto,

751
00:49:08,879 --> 00:49:12,416
has the duty to tell the truth
to the people with his own words.

752
00:49:12,482 --> 00:49:18,255
We, as the hospital, believe our feelings
are with the people of this nation.

753
00:49:20,023 --> 00:49:22,726
Who's the one that made
a big fuss about kicking him out.

754
00:49:22,793 --> 00:49:25,529
We have also heard that...

755
00:49:25,595 --> 00:49:28,532
Mayor Nioka is also
staying at this hospital.

756
00:49:28,598 --> 00:49:29,633
Yes.

757
00:49:29,700 --> 00:49:30,934
How did his surgery go?

758
00:49:31,535 --> 00:49:34,404
We heard the treatment was changed
from chemotherapy to surgery.

759
00:49:34,471 --> 00:49:35,872
Was the surgery a failure?

760
00:49:35,939 --> 00:49:37,240
What are you talking about?

761
00:49:37,741 --> 00:49:38,976
Ridiculous.

762
00:49:39,042 --> 00:49:43,513
The thing is in regards to Mayor Nioka,

763
00:49:43,947 --> 00:49:48,385
the case is entrusted
to Deputy Director Kubo.

764
00:49:48,452 --> 00:49:50,988
therefore you should hear from her.

765
00:49:51,054 --> 00:49:53,523
Huh? Wasn't she just here?

766
00:49:53,590 --> 00:49:56,893
Shoot! Michiko Daimon!

767
00:49:58,228 --> 00:49:59,830
It's all her fault.

768
00:50:03,600 --> 00:50:05,068
It's dirty!

769
00:50:05,702 --> 00:50:06,803
Yes, ma'am.

770
00:50:07,237 --> 00:50:08,772
Do it properly!

771
00:50:08,839 --> 00:50:10,040
- Yes, ma'am.
- We're sorry!

772
00:50:14,578 --> 00:50:16,179
God forbid...

773
00:50:16,713 --> 00:50:19,416
I guess she's not in the mood this time.
Excuse me.

774
00:50:29,793 --> 00:50:32,162
Why did you remove all the tumors
in the Congressman's case

775
00:50:32,229 --> 00:50:35,866
yet leave behind two in the Mayor's?
You should have been able to remove them.

776
00:50:36,900 --> 00:50:38,802
I respected his final wish.

777
00:50:45,675 --> 00:50:47,611
What a fabulous press conference it was.

778
00:50:48,111 --> 00:50:53,583
Actually I have always been photogenic,
you know.

779
00:50:54,251 --> 00:50:57,821
This will enable out University Hospital
to save its brand.

780
00:50:57,888 --> 00:50:58,855
I suppose.

781
00:50:58,922 --> 00:51:02,726
There is nothing more to say than that
it was a splendid baton of command.

782
00:51:03,760 --> 00:51:08,398
Well, this should keep that old lady Kubo
quiet for a while at least.

783
00:51:08,465 --> 00:51:13,070
There's no way she can publish that
the part-timer has failed the surgery.

784
00:51:13,136 --> 00:51:15,939
I could never take responsibility

785
00:51:16,006 --> 00:51:17,908
for anything like that.

786
00:51:17,974 --> 00:51:18,809
Yes sir.

787
00:51:18,875 --> 00:51:20,043
Yes sir.

788
00:51:20,110 --> 00:51:23,013
Saionji, your voice
just now was a little quiet.

789
00:51:23,413 --> 00:51:25,415
Repeat it a little louder.

790
00:51:26,550 --> 00:51:27,384
Yes sir.

791
00:51:27,451 --> 00:51:30,253
That was great.

792
00:51:30,787 --> 00:51:31,855
It includes this.

793
00:51:34,758 --> 00:51:35,992
Excuse me.

794
00:51:37,561 --> 00:51:40,797
Thank you very much
for hiring Dr. Daimon and

795
00:51:40,864 --> 00:51:42,566
Dr. Jonouchi this time.

796
00:51:42,632 --> 00:51:46,002
Wait a moment. I don't recall using her.

797
00:51:46,069 --> 00:51:46,903
These are melons.

798
00:51:47,270 --> 00:51:49,072
This one is Congressman Kanemoto.

799
00:51:49,873 --> 00:51:52,175
This one is Headman Nioka.

800
00:51:52,843 --> 00:51:53,677
Naturally,

801
00:51:54,244 --> 00:51:58,548
I have prepared two bills as well.

802
00:51:59,249 --> 00:52:02,185
Don't you think your greediness
has gone too far?

803
00:52:02,252 --> 00:52:06,957
Your beloved Dr. Michiko Daimon,
failed the case.

804
00:52:07,023 --> 00:52:07,858
You should know.

805
00:52:07,924 --> 00:52:10,227
I don't plan to pay a cent
to you this time.

806
00:52:10,293 --> 00:52:12,729
There is no such thing as failure
for our Daimon.

807
00:52:12,796 --> 00:52:15,332
She did leave the tumours in Mayor Nioka!

808
00:52:15,398 --> 00:52:17,134
Stop talking nonsense!

809
00:52:17,567 --> 00:52:20,804
Well then, shall we cut the nonsense and

810
00:52:21,171 --> 00:52:24,407
get right to the point.

811
00:52:25,275 --> 00:52:30,113
Dr. Daimon, left those tumours on purpose.

812
00:52:30,914 --> 00:52:31,781
What? On purpose?

813
00:52:31,848 --> 00:52:33,483
The tumor on the

814
00:52:33,550 --> 00:52:35,719
transverse colon she removed,

815
00:52:36,219 --> 00:52:38,822
had already been spread to the lymph node,

816
00:52:38,889 --> 00:52:41,158
and to protruding into
the intestinal lumen,

817
00:52:41,224 --> 00:52:43,860
creating the danger
of intestinal blockage.

818
00:52:45,228 --> 00:52:47,364
That was why she removed it!

819
00:52:47,430 --> 00:52:51,201
However, the two tumours she left

820
00:52:51,535 --> 00:52:55,138
were early stage cancer
that remained in the mucosal layer.

821
00:52:55,839 --> 00:52:59,609
Therefore, they can easily be removed

822
00:52:59,676 --> 00:53:02,746
by colorectal ESD using a colonoscope.

823
00:53:04,548 --> 00:53:07,317
For an elderly patient,
such as in this case,

824
00:53:07,384 --> 00:53:12,722
cutting out all of the tumours
from the rectum and colon at once,

825
00:53:13,089 --> 00:53:15,091
would have taken
too much a toll on the body.

826
00:53:15,625 --> 00:53:18,562
Hence, in order to protect his life,

827
00:53:19,596 --> 00:53:26,002
she has chosen the method that
involves minimal surgery.

828
00:53:30,907 --> 00:53:32,075
Gosh, you scared me.

829
00:53:32,142 --> 00:53:33,877
I apologise.

830
00:53:34,444 --> 00:53:37,681
This was like preaching
to the choir, wasn't it.

831
00:53:40,317 --> 00:53:42,385
So with that,

832
00:53:45,922 --> 00:53:49,659
please take these.

833
00:53:51,828 --> 00:53:52,729
Goodness.

834
00:53:52,796 --> 00:53:54,164
It's nonsense!

835
00:53:54,231 --> 00:53:55,732
What is this!

836
00:53:55,799 --> 00:53:58,101
Ridiculous amount of money!

837
00:53:58,168 --> 00:54:00,237
I can't believe it.

838
00:54:00,637 --> 00:54:01,938
Is this normal in Tokyo?

839
00:54:02,472 --> 00:54:08,211
If you do not pay the fees,
I will have it sent again another time.

840
00:54:08,612 --> 00:54:10,780
However,

841
00:54:11,248 --> 00:54:14,184
there is a chance that at that time,

842
00:54:14,618 --> 00:54:17,554
the sum may have shot up
two or three times.

843
00:54:17,988 --> 00:54:19,256
It will go up?

844
00:54:19,823 --> 00:54:23,326
Once we announce the success
of the Mayor's surgery,

845
00:54:23,393 --> 00:54:25,962
this hospital's ranking
will shoot up as well.

846
00:54:26,029 --> 00:54:27,097
Is that what you are trying to say?

847
00:54:27,163 --> 00:54:31,901
I'm impressed. This PR Manager
seems to understand quite well.

848
00:54:45,615 --> 00:54:46,916
Akira!

849
00:54:48,051 --> 00:54:49,185
Oh, Michiko!

850
00:54:50,720 --> 00:54:53,323
Good job. You did really great.

851
00:54:53,890 --> 00:54:55,225
Are you up for Korean BBQ?

852
00:54:55,292 --> 00:54:57,160
Yes, an expensive one.

853
00:54:57,227 --> 00:55:00,430
Sure. Today everything
will be specially selected.

854
00:55:00,497 --> 00:55:02,198
Specially selected!

855
00:55:02,632 --> 00:55:05,769
This is the story of
a lone wolf woman doctor.

856
00:55:06,569 --> 00:55:08,138
Dr. Daimon,

857
00:55:11,608 --> 00:55:13,977
I appreciate your help
with my husband's case.

858
00:55:14,044 --> 00:55:16,446
He is feeling much better.

859
00:55:16,780 --> 00:55:19,182
Did you make it to
your daughter's wedding?

860
00:55:19,683 --> 00:55:21,451
Yes. Thanks to you.

861
00:55:21,518 --> 00:55:24,387
I'm so glad! I kept my promise.

862
00:55:25,021 --> 00:55:28,658
There is a wedding.
My daughter is waiting for me.

863
00:55:31,094 --> 00:55:33,229
Oh, so that's why you don't want to
be hospitalized for a long time.

864
00:55:33,697 --> 00:55:35,632
This is my last wish.

865
00:55:37,367 --> 00:55:38,401
Got it.

866
00:55:38,468 --> 00:55:39,769
Leave it to me!

867
00:55:40,303 --> 00:55:43,340
I never fail.

868
00:55:44,507 --> 00:55:45,975
We are glad to hear that.

869
00:55:46,476 --> 00:55:48,611
I'm sure your daughter
was very happy as well.

870
00:55:50,080 --> 00:55:52,916
I actually wanted you to remove
all of the tumours.

871
00:55:53,650 --> 00:55:54,484
What?

872
00:55:54,551 --> 00:55:58,455
Even if she is his daughter,
she is from an outside relationship.

873
00:55:58,955 --> 00:56:00,056
An outside relationship?

874
00:56:02,826 --> 00:56:05,328
She's the child of his mistress.

875
00:56:07,664 --> 00:56:08,565
Seriously?

876
00:56:13,436 --> 00:56:14,270
Congratulations.

877
00:56:18,975 --> 00:56:21,911
Congratulations!

878
00:56:23,346 --> 00:56:24,180
Congratulations.

879
00:56:24,748 --> 00:56:27,083
Us as a couple, do not have any children.

880
00:56:27,150 --> 00:56:30,887
That is why I wanted him
to be hospitalized.

881
00:56:31,354 --> 00:56:35,058
But you took things too far!

882
00:56:37,861 --> 00:56:39,696
We are very sorry!

883
00:56:40,263 --> 00:56:43,400
- Akira...
- Michiko, I say this is a failure.

884
00:56:44,100 --> 00:56:46,035
No more Korean BBQ.

885
00:56:47,504 --> 00:56:49,205
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

886
00:56:50,106 --> 00:56:54,010
<i>She hates groups, authority</i>
<i>and being controlled.</i>

887
00:56:55,044 --> 00:56:59,783
<i>Her medical license and experience are</i>
<i>her only weapons.</i>

888
00:57:00,450 --> 00:57:02,952
MICHIKO DAIMON

889
00:57:05,488 --> 00:57:07,924
MICHIKO DAIMON

890
00:57:11,161 --> 00:57:14,130
PERFORMANCE RANKING: XX

891
00:57:27,343 --> 00:57:29,779
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

892
00:57:30,246 --> 00:57:31,080
<i>Also known as</i>

893
00:57:31,948 --> 00:57:33,550
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

894
00:58:50,927 --> 00:58:53,796
Are you in a relationship with a patient?

895
00:58:55,198 --> 00:58:59,569
- Please!
- I'm going to die, aren't I?

896
00:58:59,636 --> 00:59:01,671
Wait! Let go of me!

897
00:59:01,738 --> 00:59:03,940
Michiko Daimon, you failed already.

898
00:59:04,007 --> 00:59:05,475
I never fail.
